, \"quote\": \"| C1 (G1 group only): 1 \u00b5F/6.3 V | C2 = 1 \u00b5F/6.3 V | Matches G1-specific value |\"}], \"impact\": \"The panel's VDD/VDDIO rail gets less bulk capacitance than the reference design intends (0.1 \u00b5F instead of 1 \u00b5F). This can cause supply droop or ripple during EPD refresh and boost-converter switching.\", \"confidence\": 0.35}]], \"summary\": \"C11 is a 0.1 uF capacitor with an inductor footprint and one pad floating, which breaks its intended decoupling function. C1 on the EPD power rail is 0.1 uF/16V where the specification indicates 1 uF; both are reported with moderate confidence.\"}",
